  [PASS] 5-D1 THE UNIFORM CENSUS CORRECTION, CORRECTED.  An earlier version of this script asserted it was NOT absorbable into a_0 and a later one asserted it was a pure null; BOTH were wrong and the check that caught them is 5-T2.  The truth is in between and is set by T1/T2: with a_0 refitted the way the framework refits it (the deep tail), a uniform factor moves kappa by 1/f, buys back only the (f-1)sqrt(y)/2 leak -- real in the cluster CORES, negligible in the deep group and R500 rows -- and pays for it with the RAR   (kappa 0.483 -> 0.047 (fitted value 0.482 +- 0.081, so this is a 5.4 sigma move in the ONE constant the framework has); cluster |B| 0.337 -> 0.261; galaxy |B| 0.199 -> 0.539; RAR scatter 0.1271 -> 0.2648)
  [PASS] 5-D2 the gas-traced law is the one with a real physical motivation -- clusters are gas-dominated and galaxies are not, so a missing gas phase is differential in exactly the right direction.  It does close most of the cluster front.  What it costs is the RAR: it writes a gas-fraction-dependent residual into SPARC that is not observed, and it moves kappa   (cluster |B| falls 0.337 -> 0.199, but the RAR residual acquires a slope of -0.340 dex per unit gas fraction against the baseline -0.058, the RAR scatter goes 0.1271 -> 0.1570, and kappa goes 0.483 -> 0.140)
  [PASS] 5-D4 the star-traced (bottom-heavy IMF) law is worse, because clusters are only 5-15 per cent stars: buying a factor 3-4 there costs a factor of order 13 in Upsilon, and SPARC galaxies are majority stars   (fitted A = 13.2, i.e. Upsilon x14 in a purely stellar system; RAR gas-fraction slope +1.363 vs -0.058, RAR scatter 0.4374 vs 0.1271, kappa 0.005)
  [PASS] 5-D7 the only law that closes the clusters AND breaks no keeper is the one switched off in galaxies BY HAND.  It is keeper-safe precisely because it is not a law: it is one free amount applied to one class of object, and it predicts nothing about any system it was not fitted to   (every SPARC keeper identical to baseline to machine precision; cluster |B| 0.337 -> 0.069; galaxy |B| unchanged at 0.195)
  [PASS] 5-none NO LAW IN THE TABLE CLOSES BOTH HALVES.  Every law that leaves the galaxy rows alone leaves the cluster rows open, and every law that closes the cluster rows moves the galaxy rows, breaks a keeper, or both.  The minimum median residual over the galaxy rows across all nine laws is above the ledger's own 0.1 dex bar   (best galaxy-side residual over the nine laws = 0.195 dex (baseline 0.199); best cluster-side = 0.069 dex (baseline 0.337))


