  THE 1/r LENSING LAW (keeper 6).  Deep in MOND g_lens = sqrt(G M_b a_0)/r.  A baryon factor f that is CONSTANT
  in radius leaves the slope at -1 exactly and moves the amplitude by sqrt(f); a factor that VARIES with radius
  changes the slope by -d log f/d log r / 2.  The required cluster profile of section 1c has
  d log M_x/d log r = +1.353 against the gas's +1.917, so a cluster-calibrated
  radius-dependent component is NOT slope-neutral where it acts.
  [PASS] 5-lensing the 1/r law survives only the radius-INDEPENDENT laws.  Since section 1c shows the required cluster component must be radius-dependent (it is more concentrated than the gas), the law that fits the clusters is the one that would bend the lensing slope, and the law that preserves the slope is the one that does not fit the clusters   (required component slope +1.353 vs gas +1.917, a difference of 0.564 in d log M/d log r)

